1
00:00:02,222 --> 00:00:07,261
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 2

2
00:00:07,691 --> 00:00:09,761
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:16,402
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:16,714 --> 00:00:19,003
We're talking about the Battle of Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

5
00:00:19,439 --> 00:00:23,426
and we talked about the story of one woman.

6
00:00:24,253 --> 00:00:30,341
She's Zainab Bint Al-Haris(زينب بنت حارث), who tried to poison Rasool Allah ﷺ, we talked about her story.

7
00:00:30,381 --> 00:00:31,515
 So, on the other side,

8
00:00:31,878 --> 00:00:34,161
Let's talk about the story of Safiyyah Bint Huyaee(صفيه بنت حيئي).

9
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:38,643
Saffiyya Bint Huyaee رضي الله عنها remembers

10
00:00:38,683 --> 00:00:43,855
she recalls an incident that happened while she was very young girl,

11
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:50,758
and she recalls it, she reported that when Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina.

12
00:00:51,576 --> 00:00:57,277
 And he was welcomed and greeted by Al-Aos Wal Khazraj(ألأوس وَالْخَزرَج), the Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

13
00:00:58,327 --> 00:01:02,362
She says that, whenever her father or her uncle would see her.

14
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:06,122
They would play with her and smile to her

15
00:01:06,168 --> 00:01:11,884
and as you would do with the young child, beautiful child.

16
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:17,565
However, that particular day when she went, both of them were sitting under a tree,

17
00:01:17,851 --> 00:01:21,858
when she went to them, she said: They didn't welcome me as they usually do.

18
00:01:22,288 --> 00:01:26,880
And then I heard my uncle, asked my father and say: Is it him.?

19
00:01:27,508 --> 00:01:29,238
My father said: Yes.

20
00:01:29,874 --> 00:01:31,541
 He said: Are you sure it's him.?

21
00:01:31,953 --> 00:01:33,624
My father said: Yes.

22
00:01:34,063 --> 00:01:37,873
So, my uncle said: So, what are you going to do.?

23
00:01:38,294 --> 00:01:40,691
He said, or what do you think about him.

24
00:01:41,110 --> 00:01:41,492
He said;

25
00:01:41,532 --> 00:01:44,080
عَدَاوَتُه’ وَالَلهِ مَاحِّيْتَ

26
00:01:44,568 --> 00:01:47,739
I will be his enemy, as long as I live.

27
00:01:48,557 --> 00:01:54,863
And Huyaee Bin Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب) did live up to this vow of his,

28
00:01:55,115 --> 00:02:00,662
and he was the enemy of Rasool Allah ﷺ until he was killed.

29
00:02:02,073 --> 00:02:03,857
This was at the time of Hijrah(هجرة).

30
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:11,676
Three years later, Rasool Allah ﷺ would besiege, fortresses of Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير),

31
00:02:11,877 --> 00:02:15,691
 the people of Huyaee Bin Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب), whom he was their leader.

32
00:02:16,735 --> 00:02:19,271
And they would be evicted.

33
00:02:19,763 --> 00:02:22,602
So, they would move to Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

34
00:02:23,055 --> 00:02:26,578
Safiyyah(صفيه) at the time, was a young girl.

35
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:32,839
Then following that, in the fifth year of Hijrah(هجرة), it is Huyaee Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب),

36
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:41,963
 who convinces the third and last tribe of the Jews in Madina Bannu Quraidha(بنُوْ قُرَيْظَه) to betray Rasool Allah ﷺ

37
00:02:42,016 --> 00:02:45,447
and break the contract that they had,

38
00:02:46,098 --> 00:02:51,725
this contract that Rasool Allah ﷺ had with the Jews, from the time he entered into Madina.

39
00:02:52,497 --> 00:02:58,327
He is the one, who convinced them to betrayal Rasool Allah ﷺ and commit this treason.

40
00:02:58,818 --> 00:03:05,660
And we know the story, they were defeated and they were all executed, including Huyaee Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب).

41
00:03:06,652 --> 00:03:11,763
Safiyyah(صفيه) grew up in Khaybar(خَيْبَر), and she ended up marrying one of her cousins,

42
00:03:12,081 --> 00:03:13,563
Kananah Ibn Abi Al-Haqiq(كنانه إبن ابي الحقيق).

43
00:03:14,995 --> 00:03:20,317
And now, Rasool Allah ﷺ defeated the people of Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

44
00:03:20,519 --> 00:03:24,890
and the agreement between him and them was that,

45
00:03:25,575 --> 00:03:28,931
that all of their properties confiscated by the Muslims,

46
00:03:29,471 --> 00:03:32,467
and that they are to leave Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

47
00:03:33,538 --> 00:03:43,068
So, gold, silver, women, children, land, houses, all of this is transferred into the hands of the Muslims.

48
00:03:44,403 --> 00:03:48,212
But the Jews than pleaded with Rasool Allah ﷺ to allow them

49
00:03:48,927 --> 00:03:54,901
to remain in Khaybar(خَيْبَر) and serve as workers, farming and cultivating the land.

50
00:03:54,981 --> 00:03:56,720
 And the narrator of the story says;

51
00:03:57,181 --> 00:03:59,140
وَكَانُوْلَا يَفْرَغُوْنَ اَنْ يَقُوْمُوْا عَلَيْهَا

52
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:03,584
 He said that the Sahabah(صحابه), did not have time to take care of the lands, themselves.

53
00:04:03,966 --> 00:04:07,852
So, what would happen is if the Jews leave, these lands would stop producing

54
00:04:07,892 --> 00:04:09,441
 because nobody's taking care of them.

55
00:04:09,727 --> 00:04:15,082
Why? Because the Sahabah(صحابه) were busy with Ilm(علم), knowledge, Da'wah(دعوة), calling to Islam

56
00:04:15,122 --> 00:04:16,583
 and Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

57
00:04:17,456 --> 00:04:19,051
Rasool Allah ﷺ agreed.

58
00:04:19,683 --> 00:04:23,310
And the terms of the agreement were, that they would remain in Khaybar(خَيْبَر)

59
00:04:23,573 --> 00:04:25,533
and the harvest would be split in half.

60
00:04:26,844 --> 00:04:31,982
And he told them, that they should not conceal anything from him.

61
00:04:32,707 --> 00:04:38,136
All of the currency that is in their possession needs to be handed over to the Muslims

62
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:40,972
and they are not conceal anything and they agreed.

63
00:04:41,443 --> 00:04:48,189
And Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, that if we find out that you have concealed anything,

64
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:52,472
then we will punish you as we see fit and we are free from all obligations.

65
00:04:53,342 --> 00:05:00,129
They agreed to that, when they handed over their property to Rasool Allah ﷺ, it was missing.

66
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:04,920
Rasool Allah ﷺ had some inside information

67
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:10,794
about treasure that was taken by Huyaee Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب) from Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) to Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

68
00:05:11,392 --> 00:05:15,757
So, he asked them, he said: Where is the treasure of a Huyaee Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب)?

69
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,452
So, Kananah(كنانه) said;

70
00:05:17,801 --> 00:05:19,903
اَذْهَبَتْهُ الْحُرُوْبْ وَالنفقاتْ

71
00:05:20,259 --> 00:05:23,323
It was spent on war, and provisions.

72
00:05:23,696 --> 00:05:25,229
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

73
00:05:25,556 --> 00:05:28,020
اَلْعهَد قَرِيْبْ وَالْمَالْ اَكْثَرْ مِنْ ذَالِكْ

74
00:05:28,696 --> 00:05:32,944
This money couldn't have been spent, because it's a large amount of money,

75
00:05:33,182 --> 00:05:35,453
and this happened just recently.

76
00:05:35,776 --> 00:05:37,856
Kananah(كنانه) insisted that there's nothing left.

77
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:41,116
And that particular money, that belong to Huyaee Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب) was spent.

78
00:05:42,417 --> 00:05:45,767
But there was an old Jew, who said;

79
00:05:45,807 --> 00:05:52,294
I've seen Huyaee Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب) roaming around in this particular area, an area where nobody lives, Kharbah(خربه).

80
00:05:53,302 --> 00:05:56,965
So, when the Sahabah(صحابه) dug in that particular area, they found part of the money.

81
00:05:57,446 --> 00:05:59,343
They found some of it, some of this treasure,

82
00:05:59,921 --> 00:06:03,882
so Rasool Allah ﷺ told Kananah(كنانه): Where's the rest of it, Kananah(كنانه) refused to admit.

83
00:06:04,129 --> 00:06:07,384
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ handed him over to Az-Zubair Bin Awaam(زبير بن عوام).

84
00:06:07,625 --> 00:06:09,888
وَقَالَ عذّبْه’ حَتَّى تَستأصلْ مَا عِنْدَه

85
00:06:09,928 --> 00:06:13,607
Rough him up until you take what is left.

86
00:06:14,183 --> 00:06:23,258
So, Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) was able, in the end to extract information about where this treasure is located, the rest of it.

87
00:06:24,156 --> 00:06:30,573
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that Kananah(كنانه) be executed, and he was.

88
00:06:30,613 --> 00:06:34,920
 And Kananah(كنانه) is the husband of Safiyyah رضي الله عنها .

89
00:06:35,489 --> 00:06:38,775
Safiyyah(صفيه) was among the captives,

90
00:06:39,567 --> 00:06:43,011
and Dah'yah Al-Kalbi(دحية اَلْكَلْبِي) one of the Sahabah(صحابه).

91
00:06:43,531 --> 00:06:48,046
He came to Rasool Allah ﷺ asking for a slave.

92
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:52,354
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ handed him over Safiyyah(صفيه),

93
00:06:52,837 --> 00:06:55,743
because that was the rule at that time in the world,

94
00:06:55,783 --> 00:06:57,390
 this is not something that the Muslims brought,

95
00:06:57,508 --> 00:06:58,860
that's the way things were.

96
00:06:59,302 --> 00:07:03,684
Muslims came, on the international scene and this is how it was,

97
00:07:04,889 --> 00:07:09,788
that women and children, if they fall into custody after war,

98
00:07:10,191 --> 00:07:12,249
they are automatically enslaved.

99
00:07:12,651 --> 00:07:16,643
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him go and choose a woman, that you like,

100
00:07:16,723 --> 00:07:19,178
 so he went and he, and he took Safiyyah(صفيه).

101
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:23,900
She was described as being very beautiful so, he ended up choosing her.

102
00:07:24,146 --> 00:07:27,098
So, one of the Sahabah(صحابه) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him

103
00:07:27,378 --> 00:07:34,362
that Dah'yah(دحية) has taken Safiyyah(صفيه), the daughter of the noble man of Al-Yahood(اليهود),

104
00:07:34,654 --> 00:07:38,901
and she is only be fitting to be yours, O Messenger of Allah.

105
00:07:39,402 --> 00:07:41,728
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ called Dah'yah(دحية) and told him;

106
00:07:41,785 --> 00:07:45,348
Hand over Safiyyah(صفيه), and go and take someone else.

107
00:07:45,594 --> 00:07:47,136
Dah'yah(دحية) did so.

108
00:07:47,390 --> 00:07:51,275
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he saw Safiyah رضي الله عنها .

109
00:07:51,557 --> 00:07:56,793
He offered her freedom as Mahar(مهر), and he would marry her.

110
00:07:57,333 --> 00:07:59,616
So, he did not take her as a slave.

111
00:07:59,902 --> 00:08:09,329
But he freed her and married her, so she is counted as a wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ, and not a woman who is in bondage.

112
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:10,980
She was not,

113
00:08:11,091 --> 00:08:13,035
مِمَّا مَلَكَتْ يَمِيْنُه

114
00:08:14,495 --> 00:08:19,483
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw some blue marks in her face.

115
00:08:20,397 --> 00:08:23,036
He asked her, What is this.?

116
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:27,297
She said: One day I was sleeping.

117
00:08:27,552 --> 00:08:29,734
My head was in the lap of my husband

118
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,480
and I saw a dream.

119
00:08:32,065 --> 00:08:34,954
I saw the moon falling in my lap.

120
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:39,393
When I woke up I told my husband about this dream.

121
00:08:39,915 --> 00:08:42,436
My husband slapped me, in the face and said;

122
00:08:42,848 --> 00:08:45,190
You desire the king of the Arabs.

123
00:08:45,682 --> 00:08:52,266
So, Kananah(كنانه) interpreted this dream to mean, that she is desiring to marry Muhammadﷺ.

124
00:08:52,602 --> 00:08:54,549
It wasn't a desire that she had,

125
00:08:54,943 --> 00:08:59,880
this is a dream, that is true dream, it is from Allahعَزّوجَلّ

126
00:09:00,123 --> 00:09:03,266
and it is telling her, what will happen in the future,

127
00:09:03,464 --> 00:09:10,000
and it happened, as it was interpreted that she would marry Muhammadﷺ.

128
00:09:11,126 --> 00:09:17,502
So, those blue marks in her face, where the traces of the slap from her husband Kananah(كنانه).

129
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:23,632
Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه, he narrates to us part of the story of Safiyyah(صفيه).

130
00:09:23,964 --> 00:09:27,424
And there's, this particular part that I found interesting

131
00:09:27,575 --> 00:09:31,652
and it gives us a glimpse into the private life of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

132
00:09:31,692 --> 00:09:34,859
 and how he used to deal with his family.

133
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:38,407
The camel is pretty tall animals,

134
00:09:39,184 --> 00:09:42,738
so when a person is sitting on a camel, he is quite high,

135
00:09:43,222 --> 00:09:45,953
it's higher than riding on a horse.

136
00:09:46,663 --> 00:09:51,801
So, when people would ride on a camel, the camel must be sitting down, but even then, it's still a bit high.

137
00:09:52,429 --> 00:09:57,303
Anas Ibn Malik(اَنَس ابن مالك) said: I saw Rasool Allah ﷺ sit down on the ground,

138
00:09:57,662 --> 00:10:02,156
with his foot on the ground and then he raised up, his knee

139
00:10:02,625 --> 00:10:09,757
and told Safiyyah(صفيه) to step with her foot on his knee, in order to climb the camel.

140
00:10:10,130 --> 00:10:19,126
So, I'm sure you can sense the humbleness and the kindness and compassion that Rasool Allah ﷺ had,

141
00:10:19,628 --> 00:10:24,201
 he being as described by the Yahood(يهود) the king of the Arabs,

142
00:10:24,335 --> 00:10:26,591
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused Kingdom,

143
00:10:27,432 --> 00:10:33,010
he was offered to be a Nabi(نبي) and king and he just chose to be a Nabi(نبي) only.

144
00:10:33,374 --> 00:10:37,620
Rasool Allah ﷺ the greatest of human beings,

145
00:10:37,897 --> 00:10:41,400
the greatest man that ever set foot on this earth.

146
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:48,840
He sits down on the ground and has his wife step over him,

147
00:10:49,087 --> 00:10:51,444
in order to climb that camel.

148
00:10:52,721 --> 00:10:56,793
And Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to soften the hearts of Safiyyah(صفيه),

149
00:10:56,833 --> 00:11:02,847
because naturally Safiyyah(صفيه), her father was killed, her uncle was killed,

150
00:11:02,977 --> 00:11:05,934
and her husband killed, all by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

151
00:11:06,296 --> 00:11:10,237
and she saw the complete annihilation of her people,

152
00:11:10,729 --> 00:11:15,614
the eviction of them from the Arabian Peninsula.

153
00:11:15,694 --> 00:11:21,561
All of these events occurred in front of her eyes during her lifetime and she was a young woman at the time.

154
00:11:21,804 --> 00:11:25,274
So, she must have had some hard feelings because of that.

155
00:11:25,701 --> 00:11:26,631
And she said;

156
00:11:27,261 --> 00:11:30,176
وَكَانَ رَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم منْ اَبْغَضَ النَّاسَ الَيْه

157
00:11:30,531 --> 00:11:35,175
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the most despised of people to me.

158
00:11:35,725 --> 00:11:37,973
He killed my husband, and my father.

159
00:11:38,157 --> 00:11:40,248
فَمَا زالَ يَعْتَذر إلي

160
00:11:40,672 --> 00:11:43,538
And he would apologize to me and say;

161
00:11:43,804 --> 00:11:48,863
اِنَّ اَبَاكِ علب عَلَيَّ الْعَرَبْ وَفَعَلَ وَفَعَلْ حَتَّى ذَهَبَ ذَالِكَ مِنْ نَفْسِيْ

162
00:11:49,081 --> 00:11:52,268
And he continued apologizing to me, and telling me

163
00:11:52,387 --> 00:11:55,543
that your father is the one, who mobilize the Arabs against me,

164
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:59,041
and he's the one, who did so and so, and he did this and that

165
00:11:59,572 --> 00:12:03,360
until, all of the pain in my heart was taken away.

166
00:12:03,770 --> 00:12:09,931
And this is how Rasool Allah ﷺ won the heart of Safiyyah رضي الله عنها,

167
00:12:10,252 --> 00:12:14,661
she is Umm-Ul-Mo'mineen(إم المؤمنين), may Allah be pleased with her.

168
00:12:15,141 --> 00:12:16,695
This is the story of Safiyyah(صفيه).

169
00:12:17,316 --> 00:12:19,527
Another incident that occurred,

170
00:12:20,353 --> 00:12:25,157
there was a servant of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

171
00:12:26,383 --> 00:12:30,442
He was struck by an arrow and he died,

172
00:12:31,821 --> 00:12:33,249
so the Sahabah(صحابه) said;

173
00:12:33,368 --> 00:12:35,780
 اَلشَّهِيْد، اَلشَّهِيْد،هَنيئا له بِشَّهَادَةْ

174
00:12:35,811 --> 00:12:39,860
Congratulations on dying as a martyr.

175
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:41,721
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

176
00:12:41,855 --> 00:12:52,219
كَلَّا وَالَّذِيْ نَفْسِيْ بِيَدِهْ، اِنَّ الشَمْلَة الَّتِيْ اَصَابَهَا يَوْمَ خَيْبَرْ لَمْ تُصِبْهَا الْمَقَاسِمْ لَتَشْتَعِلُ عَلَيْهِ نَارًا

177
00:12:52,946 --> 00:12:55,320
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No,

178
00:12:55,965 --> 00:13:01,160
by the name of the One, Whom my soul is in His hands.

179
00:13:01,827 --> 00:13:05,778
The cloak that he has taken on the day of Khaybar(خَيْبَر)

180
00:13:06,549 --> 00:13:10,861
from the Ghaneemah(غنيمه) is burning on him, flames.

181
00:13:12,170 --> 00:13:13,516
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

182
00:13:13,777 --> 00:13:21,146
So, that cloak is burning him, a single piece of cloth that was taken from the Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

183
00:13:21,579 --> 00:13:25,697
This is a Muslim, a Mo'min(مؤمن), a Mujahid(مجاهد)

184
00:13:26,404 --> 00:13:28,842
and a person who died Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

185
00:13:29,573 --> 00:13:34,241
but Rasool Allah ﷺ refused to pray Janazah(جنازه) for him

186
00:13:34,553 --> 00:13:37,269
and he said: No, he's not a Shaheed(شهيد).

187
00:13:37,349 --> 00:13:37,695
Why?

188
00:13:37,735 --> 00:13:40,124
Because of that cloak that he has taken.

189
00:13:40,635 --> 00:13:45,720
So, this is how dangerous it is to take anything from Al-Ghaneemah(ألغنيمه).

190
00:13:46,259 --> 00:13:48,603
Also in the Battle of Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

191
00:13:49,045 --> 00:13:52,399
when the Muslims were laying siege to some of the fortresses,

192
00:13:53,055 --> 00:13:54,801
they were very hungry,

193
00:13:55,283 --> 00:13:58,525
so they ended up slaughtering donkeys and cooking them.

194
00:13:58,565 --> 00:14:01,883
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, What is boiling in these pots?

195
00:14:01,963 --> 00:14:02,711
They said;

196
00:14:02,995 --> 00:14:04,046
حمر الاهلية

197
00:14:04,257 --> 00:14:06,221
We slaughtered some donkeys.

198
00:14:06,443 --> 00:14:09,301
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Throw it all away,

199
00:14:09,565 --> 00:14:14,697
and that is when, Rasool Allah ﷺ made the eating of the flesh of donkeys, Haraam(حرام).

200
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:18,874
It was something, that the Arabs would do before that but Islam made it Haraam(حرام).

201
00:14:18,947 --> 00:14:22,479
 So, it's not allowed to eat the flesh of donkeys.

202
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:25,185
 It was made Haraam(حرام) during the Battle of Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

203
00:14:25,748 --> 00:14:30,430
The Jews remained in Khaybar(خَيْبَر) serving in the land

204
00:14:31,266 --> 00:14:37,433
and the Muslims would send someone, to collect the 50% of the harvest.

205
00:14:37,738 --> 00:14:41,062
So, once Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) is the one, who went to them.

206
00:14:41,142 --> 00:14:44,576
 So, they tried to bribe him,

207
00:14:45,057 --> 00:14:48,063
and this shows you, the corruption of Al-Yahood(أليهود).

208
00:14:48,568 --> 00:14:52,245
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) was very rough with them, when they did this

209
00:14:52,727 --> 00:14:54,711
and he made it clear to them,

210
00:14:55,016 --> 00:14:57,981
that I would not betray the trust of Rasool Allah ﷺ

211
00:14:58,005 --> 00:15:00,970
no matter what you try to do, no matter what you give me.

212
00:15:01,568 --> 00:15:03,917
They remained in Khaybar(خَيْبَر)

213
00:15:04,068 --> 00:15:07,655
until the time of Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه when he was Khalifah(خليفه).

214
00:15:08,123 --> 00:15:15,315
Al-Miqdaad(المقداد) and Az-Zubair(الزبير) and Ibn Umar(ابن عمر), they went to Khaybar(خَيْبَر) to collect their shares

215
00:15:15,998 --> 00:15:21,426
 and the Yahood(يهود) attacked Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) at night

216
00:15:21,823 --> 00:15:26,104
and they pushed him from a roof, he was sleeping on a roof,

217
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:30,096
they pushed him and he fell down and he dislocated both hands.

218
00:15:30,681 --> 00:15:33,093
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه said;

219
00:15:33,387 --> 00:15:35,736
O people, he is speaking to the Muslims.

220
00:15:35,776 --> 00:15:41,135
He said: O people, the Messenger of Allah had an agreement with the Jews of Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

221
00:15:41,437 --> 00:15:44,229
that we should evict them if we wished.

222
00:15:44,831 --> 00:15:49,324
So, the agreement that I had with them is that you stay and you serve in the farms.

223
00:15:49,372 --> 00:15:54,979
 However,it's up to us, whenever we want to evict you, we can evict you.

224
00:15:55,733 --> 00:15:57,548
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: O people;

225
00:15:57,767 --> 00:16:01,893
The Messenger of Allah had an agreement with the Jews of Khaybar(خيبر)

226
00:16:02,158 --> 00:16:04,281
that we should evict them if we wished.

227
00:16:04,698 --> 00:16:10,078
They have attacked Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) and dislocated his hands, as you have learned,

228
00:16:10,531 --> 00:16:13,110
having attacked one of the Ansaar(أنْصَار) before him.

229
00:16:13,372 --> 00:16:16,237
We have no doubt, that it was they who did it.

230
00:16:16,681 --> 00:16:19,038
We have no enemies here, besides them.

231
00:16:19,293 --> 00:16:23,091
Those who have property at Khaybar(خَيْبَر) should proceed to them,

232
00:16:23,392 --> 00:16:25,376
 I'm going to evict the Jews.

233
00:16:26,048 --> 00:16:29,749
And they were forced to leave and they went to Ash-sham(الشام).

234
00:16:29,971 --> 00:16:35,287
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), one of the reasons that he did this is

235
00:16:35,582 --> 00:16:41,484
the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ  that no two religions should exist in the Arabian Peninsula

236
00:16:41,848 --> 00:16:47,178
and the Hadith(حديث) drive the Jews and the Christians out of the Arabian Peninsula

237
00:16:47,610 --> 00:16:52,168
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) even though he didn't hear this Hadith(حديث) directly from Rasool Allah ﷺ,

238
00:16:52,213 --> 00:16:55,784
 he investigated it and found it to be authentic and true.

239
00:16:55,958 --> 00:17:03,324
And he acted upon it, and drove the Yahood(يهود) of Khaybar(خَيْبَر) out of the Arabian Peninsula to Ash-Sham(الشام).

240
00:17:04,056 --> 00:17:10,405
300 years later, these Yahood(يهود), their descendants, who were in Ash-sham(الشام)

241
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:13,183
they wrote up a document

242
00:17:14,093 --> 00:17:19,806
stating that, this was an agreement between them and Rasool Allah ﷺ that, they are Jizya(جزية) free.

243
00:17:19,886 --> 00:17:21,109
 They don't have to pay Jizya(جزية),

244
00:17:21,521 --> 00:17:22,971
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), he says;

245
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:27,819
And this document has fooled, some of the scholars to believe it

246
00:17:28,494 --> 00:17:32,545
and I have investigated it and found it, to be a lie and a fabrication.

247
00:17:33,004 --> 00:17:36,973
There was no such document, and the Jews, and this is 300 years later.

248
00:17:37,013 --> 00:17:41,886
I mean they didn't give up 300 years later and they're still fabricating

249
00:17:42,077 --> 00:17:47,406
and claiming that Rasool Allah ﷺ had an agreement with them that, they shouldn't pay any Jizya(جزية).

250
00:17:47,718 --> 00:17:50,073
So, the document was proven to be a fabrication.

251
00:17:50,369 --> 00:17:53,243
Then 700 years after Hijrah(هجرة),

252
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:55,714
they come up with the same document again,

253
00:17:55,754 --> 00:18:03,025
with some, probably with some alterations, and some changes and again it was proven to be a lie.

254
00:18:03,944 --> 00:18:10,153
While Rasool Allah ﷺ was at Khaybar(خَيْبَر) he received four delegations or envoys.

255
00:18:10,991 --> 00:18:13,420
The first was Wafd Al-Ashriyeen(وفد ألأشعرين).

256
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:22,043
Al-Asharieen(اَلْأشعرين) are people from Yemen from the area of Zabeed(زبيد), on the coast of the Red Sea

257
00:18:22,781 --> 00:18:27,967
 and will read what Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبومُوسى الأشْعَري) says in this Hadith(حديث) from Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري).

258
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:38,061
عن أبي موسى قال بلغنا مخرج رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ونحن باليمن فخرجنا مهاجرين إليه

259
00:18:38,358 --> 00:18:44,670
أنا وأخوان لي أنا أصغرهم أحدهما أبو بردة والآخر أبو رهم

260
00:18:45,218 --> 00:18:53,096
 إما قال بضعا وإما قال ثلاثة وخمسين أو اثنين وخمسين رجلا من قومي

261
00:18:53,534 --> 00:19:02,428
 قال فركبنا سفينة فألقتنا سفينتنا إلى النجاشي بالحبشة فوافقنا جعفر بن أبي طالب

262
00:19:02,573 --> 00:19:08,725
فأقمنا معه حتى قدمنا جميعا فوافقنا الني صلى الله عليه وسلم حين افتتح خيبر

263
00:19:09,581 --> 00:19:12,336
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari رضي الله عنه said;

264
00:19:12,644 --> 00:19:19,844
We heard the news of the Prophet Muhammadﷺ while we were in Yemen.

265
00:19:20,142 --> 00:19:27,446
So, we went out to migrate to him, me and two brothers of mine and I was their youngest,

266
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:32,768
along with 52 or 53 men from my people.

267
00:19:32,857 --> 00:19:34,391
So, this was quite a large group,

268
00:19:34,755 --> 00:19:37,140
they were all going Hijrah(هجرة) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

269
00:19:37,357 --> 00:19:40,147
when they heard the news of Muhammadﷺ.

270
00:19:40,977 --> 00:19:48,710
They took a boat, but this boat went off course and they ended up not in Madina

271
00:19:48,808 --> 00:19:51,507
but in Abyssinia, the land of An-Najashi(أنجاشي),

272
00:19:51,808 --> 00:19:53,914
so we found Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب) there.

273
00:19:54,082 --> 00:19:58,763
Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب) told us that he has instructions to remain there.

274
00:19:59,208 --> 00:20:02,477
So, he was staying there according to the instructions of Rasool Allah ﷺ

275
00:20:02,754 --> 00:20:09,413
and we stayed with him, until we came together with Jafar(جعفر), when Rasool Allah ﷺ, opened Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

276
00:20:09,487 --> 00:20:14,210
So, the next delegation then, or the next group is Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب),

277
00:20:14,330 --> 00:20:16,186
 the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) of Al-Habasha(ألحبشه).

278
00:20:17,075 --> 00:20:19,647
Why did the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) of Al-Habasha(ألحبشه) returned back.?

279
00:20:19,687 --> 00:20:21,176
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says;

280
00:20:21,299 --> 00:20:26,989
بَعَثَ الرَسول عمْرو بِنْ اُمَيَّه اَلضمَّرِيْ اِلَى النَّجَاشِيْ يَطْلُبْ مِنْهُمْ مِن بَقِي من اَصْحَابِي بِالْحَبَشَهْ

281
00:20:27,227 --> 00:20:31,832
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Amr Bin Umayyah Ad-Damri(عمرو بن أمَيَّة اَضّْمْرِيْ) to An-Najashi(أنجاشي)

282
00:20:32,101 --> 00:20:37,369
asking him, to send the remaining companions back to Madina.

283
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:44,161
Ash'habi(أشبِعي) says, that when Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب) arrived at Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

284
00:20:44,678 --> 00:20:48,670
Rasool Allah ﷺ kissed him on his forehead, and embraced him,

285
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:59,041
and this is what our scholars used as evidence of the permissibility of hugging, it is this incident.

286
00:21:00,168 --> 00:21:01,279
 This is Mursil(مُرْسَلْ) .

287
00:21:01,597 --> 00:21:03,462
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

288
00:21:03,945 --> 00:21:10,604
مَا اَدْرِيْ بِاَيِّهِمَا اَنَا اَثَرْ بِفَتْحِ خَيْبَرْ، اَمْ بِقُدُوْمِ جَعْفَرْ

289
00:21:11,041 --> 00:21:15,627
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I don't know which has brought me more joy,

290
00:21:15,969 --> 00:21:19,470
the opening of Khaybar(خَيْبَر) or the arrival of Jafar(جعفر).

291
00:21:20,151 --> 00:21:26,874
Rasool Allah ﷺ was extremely happy with the arrival of Jafar Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه,

292
00:21:27,194 --> 00:21:33,961
it has been a long time, since he last saw, his cousin Jafar Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

293
00:21:34,215 --> 00:21:37,472
We carry on with the Hadith(حديث) of Bukhari(بخاريْ) which we were reading from,

294
00:21:37,798 --> 00:21:39,393
 narrated by Abu Musa(ابوموسى).

295
00:21:39,885 --> 00:21:44,929
وَكَانَ اُنَاسٌ مِّنَّ النَّاسِ يَقُوْلُوْنَ لَنَا يَعْنِيْ لِاَهْلِ السّفِيْنَهْ سَبَقْنَاكُمْ بِالْهِجْرَةْ

296
00:21:45,224 --> 00:21:48,487
And some people used to tell us, We, the People of the boat

297
00:21:48,987 --> 00:21:52,107
that we have made Hijrah(هجرة) before you.

298
00:21:53,022 --> 00:21:59,197
وَدَخَلَتْ اَسْمَآءُ بِنْتِ عمَيْس وَهيَّ مِمَّنْ قَدِمَ مَعَنَا عَلَى حَفْصَه زَوْجَ النَّبِيْ صلى الله عليه وسلم

299
00:21:59,386 --> 00:22:02,725
Asma Bint Omais(أسماء بنت عميس), who was one of the women,

300
00:22:03,006 --> 00:22:04,959
who were the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) in Abyssinia,

301
00:22:05,558 --> 00:22:10,254
she visited Hafsa(حفصه), the daughter Umar(عُمَر), the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

302
00:22:10,761 --> 00:22:17,634
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, he came in and he saw this woman with his daughter, Hafsa(حفصه),

303
00:22:18,199 --> 00:22:20,592
so when Umar(عُمَر) saw Asmaa(أسماء), he said;

304
00:22:20,830 --> 00:22:21,830
 مَنْ هَذِه

305
00:22:22,175 --> 00:22:23,568
He said: Who is this woman.?

306
00:22:23,783 --> 00:22:26,187
Hafsa(حفصه) said: Asma Bin Omais(أسماء بنت عميس).

307
00:22:26,489 --> 00:22:27,432
Umar(عُمَر) said;

308
00:22:27,673 --> 00:22:30,478
آلْحَبَشِيَّه هَذِهْ، آلْبَحْرِيَّهْ هَذِهْ

309
00:22:30,791 --> 00:22:34,281
Is this the Abyssinian woman, is this the seafaring woman?

310
00:22:34,502 --> 00:22:36,047
Asmaa(أسماء) said: Yes.

311
00:22:36,841 --> 00:22:38,098
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

312
00:22:38,286 --> 00:22:42,888
سَبَقْنَاكُمْ بِالْهِجْرَه فَنَحْنُ اَحَقْ بِرَسُوْل الله صلى الله عليه وسلم مِنْكُمْ

313
00:22:43,145 --> 00:22:50,149
We have made Hijrah(هجرة) before you, therefore we have more right over Rasool Allah ﷺ then you.

314
00:22:50,771 --> 00:22:54,176
Meaning Rasool Allah ﷺ was closer to us or we have more right to him, then you.

315
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:57,363
Asmaa(أسماء) was quite angry with this,

316
00:22:57,781 --> 00:22:58,812
and she said: No,

317
00:22:59,069 --> 00:23:05,910
كَلَّا وَالله كُنْتُمْ مَعَ رَسُوْلِ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يُطْعِمُ جَائِعَكُمْ، وَيَعِظُ جَاهِلَكُمْ،

318
00:23:06,060 --> 00:23:11,819
وَكُنَّا في دَارِ، أَوْ في أَرْضِ البُعَدَاءِ البُغَضَاءِ في الحَبَشَةِ، وَذلكَ في اللهِ وفي رَسولِهِ

319
00:23:12,521 --> 00:23:18,982
She said: No, in the name of Allah, you were with Rasool Allah ﷺ, he was feeding the hungry among you,

320
00:23:19,193 --> 00:23:22,095
and he was advising the ignorant among you,

321
00:23:22,370 --> 00:23:27,014
and we were in a land that was disliked, and far away,

322
00:23:27,233 --> 00:23:32,952
and all of that was for the sake of Allah and the Messenger of Allah.

323
00:23:33,443 --> 00:23:41,309
وَاَيْمُ الله لَا أطْعَمُ طَعَامًا وَلَا أشْرَبُ شَرَابًا حَتَّى اَذْكُرَ مَا قلْتَ لِرَسُوْلِ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

324
00:23:41,692 --> 00:23:43,962
And in the name of Allah, I'm not going to eat anything,

325
00:23:44,066 --> 00:23:45,561
and I'm not going to drink anything,

326
00:23:45,844 --> 00:23:47,986
until I tell Rasool Allah ﷺ, what you said;

327
00:23:48,227 --> 00:23:50,470
وَنَحْنُ كُنَّا نُؤذى وَنُخَافْ

328
00:23:50,671 --> 00:23:53,457
And we were harmed, and we were in a state of fear.

329
00:23:53,835 --> 00:23:59,727
وَسَاَذْكُرُ ذَالِكَ لِنَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَاَسْئلُه’ وَاللهِ لَا اَكْذِبُ ولَا اَزيْغُ وَلَا اَزِيْدُ عَلَيْه

330
00:23:59,867 --> 00:24:01,937
And I'm going to tell him the truth, exactly.

331
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:05,469
I'm not going to add anything or subtract anything from what you said.

332
00:24:06,738 --> 00:24:10,273
So, she went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and she told him

333
00:24:10,833 --> 00:24:14,388
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said, so and so, said this is that,

334
00:24:14,984 --> 00:24:18,030
Rasool Allah ﷺ told her and what did you say?

335
00:24:18,589 --> 00:24:22,165
And she mentioned to Rasool Ullah, what her response was.

336
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,947
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say?

337
00:24:24,365 --> 00:24:26,581
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

338
00:24:27,244 --> 00:24:32,052
No, He does not have more right over me, then you do.

339
00:24:32,660 --> 00:24:38,595
He and his companions, have one Hijrah(هجرة) and you have two Hijrah(هجرة).

340
00:24:39,305 --> 00:24:43,228
Because the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) of Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه), they made Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه)

341
00:24:43,476 --> 00:24:45,034
and they made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina.

342
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:50,556
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told her; They have, the reward of one Hijrah(هجرة)

343
00:24:51,252 --> 00:24:54,832
and you have the reward of making Hijrah(هجرة) twice.

344
00:24:55,411 --> 00:25:01,179
Asma Bint Omais(أسماء بنت عميس) said: After that I would see groups and groups

345
00:25:01,862 --> 00:25:05,345
of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) who were in Abyssinia, coming to me,

346
00:25:05,537 --> 00:25:09,527
asking me, to narrate to them the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

347
00:25:09,567 --> 00:25:10,343
And she said;

348
00:25:10,529 --> 00:25:15,685
Nothing was more beloved to them in the world, than the words of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

349
00:25:15,999 --> 00:25:23,973
they were so happy, with this reward that came to them from the tongues of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

350
00:25:24,140 --> 00:25:26,585
 that everybody else has reward of one Hijrah(هجرة)

351
00:25:26,609 --> 00:25:29,232
while they have the reward of Hijrah(هجرة) twice

352
00:25:29,456 --> 00:25:35,123
that they would come in groups asking her to narrate the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Ullah to them

353
00:25:35,496 --> 00:25:36,325
 and she said;

354
00:25:36,665 --> 00:25:43,363
And I would remember, Abu Musa Al-Ashaari(ابوموسى ألأشعري) visiting me again, and again asking me to narrate the Hadith(حديث) to him.

355
00:25:43,590 --> 00:25:46,073
He wasn't satisfied with hearing it once,

356
00:25:46,351 --> 00:25:49,541
he wanted to hear it once and twice and thrice

357
00:25:49,795 --> 00:25:54,188
to hear the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ that gave them, this great Ajr(أجر).

358
00:25:54,251 --> 00:25:55,427
Brothers and Sisters,

359
00:25:55,912 --> 00:25:58,514
we should love the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

360
00:25:58,700 --> 00:26:03,766
and we should love to hear it again and again, just like Abu Musa Al-Ashaari رضي الله عنه did.

361
00:26:04,599 --> 00:26:10,274
He had probably travel and he had to come, a long way to listen to this Hadith(حديث), from Asmaa(إسماء).

362
00:26:10,398 --> 00:26:12,024
 We have the books of Hadith(حديث) with us.

363
00:26:12,088 --> 00:26:16,388
All of them, right next to us, at our fingertips.

364
00:26:16,845 --> 00:26:19,678
We should listen to the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

365
00:26:19,726 --> 00:26:27,001
we should bless our ears with listening to the words of Rasool Ullah صلوات لله وسلام عليه.

366
00:26:28,237 --> 00:26:30,985
Then there was the delegation of Addari'een(ألداريين).

367
00:26:31,288 --> 00:26:34,540
Addari'een(ألداريين) were from Ash-Sham(ألشام) from the tribe of Laham(لحم).

368
00:26:34,990 --> 00:26:36,779
They visited Rasool Allah ﷺ

369
00:26:36,804 --> 00:26:39,626
while he was in Al-Khaybar(خَيْبَر) among them was Tamim Ad-Daari(تميم ألداري).

370
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:44,150
If you remember Tamim Ad-Daari(تميم ألداري), we talked about him in the series about the hereafter.

371
00:26:44,315 --> 00:26:50,720
Tamim Ad-Daari(تميم ألداري) is the one who narrated to Rasool Allah ﷺ his story with Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال).

372
00:26:51,147 --> 00:26:56,861
When they were in the sea and the winds carried them away to this island

373
00:26:56,917 --> 00:27:00,464
and they went to this island and they found this beast covered with hair,

374
00:27:00,504 --> 00:27:02,271
 they cannot tell the front of it, from the back

375
00:27:02,764 --> 00:27:07,232
and they went into this temple and the saw, this huge man chained up

376
00:27:07,456 --> 00:27:10,571
 and he asked him some questions and then he said, that he is Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال).

377
00:27:10,909 --> 00:27:14,885
This is the one, Tamim Ad-Daari(تميم ألداري) who told Rasool Allah ﷺ, this story.

378
00:27:15,492 --> 00:27:21,112
And then there's the largest delegation, which was the Wafd(وفد) of Ad-Daus(ألدوس).

379
00:27:21,604 --> 00:27:25,342
Daus(دوس) are tribe from Yemen from Al-Azd(ألازد)

380
00:27:25,856 --> 00:27:29,483
and these are the people of Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه,

381
00:27:30,073 --> 00:27:33,527
Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) is the one, who narrated to us the story, he said: 50(Fifty)

382
00:27:33,935 --> 00:27:35,354
ثَمَانِيْنَ بَيْتَا مِنْ دَوْس

383
00:27:35,394 --> 00:27:38,664
50 houses or 50 families Allah Ho-Alam(الله اعلم) from Daus(دوس),

384
00:27:39,526 --> 00:27:45,090
they made Hijrah(هجرة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they arrived at Madina

385
00:27:45,451 --> 00:27:49,786
but they were told that Rasool Allah ﷺ was in Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

386
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:56,495
Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه said: Wherever, Rasool Allah ﷺ is, we'll go to him.

387
00:27:56,914 --> 00:27:59,683
They didn't want to wait, until Rasool Allah ﷺ comes back.

388
00:27:59,995 --> 00:28:01,735
They said: Wherever he is, we'll go.

389
00:28:02,106 --> 00:28:09,138
So, Saba Bin Ar-Fatah Al-Ghaffari(صبا بن عرفطه ألغفاري) who was appointed Ameer(أمير), on Madina provided them with provisions.

390
00:28:09,299 --> 00:28:12,362
 So, they traveled and met Rasool Allah ﷺ in Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

391
00:28:12,804 --> 00:28:15,241
And therefore we can know from this,

392
00:28:15,281 --> 00:28:20,972
that Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) and Abu Musa Al-Ashaari(ابوموسى ألْأشعري) joined, Rasool Allah ﷺ at that particular time.

393
00:28:21,294 --> 00:28:26,037
This is an important thing for, the scholars of Hadith(حديث), and the scholars of fiqh(فقه)

394
00:28:26,356 --> 00:28:32,808
because it tells them the date in which these two Sahabah(صحابه) who narrated many Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Ullah,

395
00:28:33,110 --> 00:28:34,766
 it tells them when they became Muslim,

396
00:28:34,790 --> 00:28:37,718
so they would know that the Hadith(حديث) that are narrated by them

397
00:28:38,157 --> 00:28:42,733
are Ahadith(احاديث) that were heard, after the seventh year of Hijrah(هجرة).

398
00:28:43,947 --> 00:28:51,150
On their way back, Rasool Allah ﷺ told Bilal(بلال) to wake them up for Fajr(فجر).

399
00:28:51,787 --> 00:28:57,180
Bilal(بلال) overslept and so did Rasool Allah ﷺ and so did the rest of the Sahabah(صحابه).

400
00:28:57,252 --> 00:29:00,553
They only woke up, due to the heat of the sun.

401
00:29:01,414 --> 00:29:05,561
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ woke up and he was the first among them to wake up.

402
00:29:06,291 --> 00:29:08,808
He told Bilal(بلال), what happened to you?

403
00:29:09,097 --> 00:29:11,373
Bilal(بلال) told him, the same thing that happened to you.

404
00:29:12,213 --> 00:29:17,618
They prayed then, and Rasool Allah ﷺ said, that,

405
00:29:17,830 --> 00:29:20,326
مَنْ نَسِيَ صَلَاةْ فَلْيُصَلِّيهَا اِذَ ذكَرَهَا

406
00:29:20,350 --> 00:29:23,672
When you forget about the Salah(صلاة) pray it, when you remember it.

407
00:29:24,341 --> 00:29:27,726
Same thing, if you sleep then you pray when you wake up.

408
00:29:28,273 --> 00:29:31,361
It's not like some people do if they missed Fajr(فجر),

409
00:29:31,925 --> 00:29:33,869
they would not pray it, when they would wake up

410
00:29:33,909 --> 00:29:36,814
and rather they would combine it, with the Fajr(فجر) of the next day.

411
00:29:37,183 --> 00:29:38,842
That is not the correct thing to do,

412
00:29:38,882 --> 00:29:42,112
the correct thing to do is to pray it, as soon as you wake up, with every Salah(صلاة).

413
00:29:42,588 --> 00:29:47,419
Whether it is Zohar(ظهر), Asar(عصر), Maghrib(مغرب), Isha'a(عشاء), if you sleep, then you pray it as soon as you wake up.

414
00:29:48,591 --> 00:29:51,570
Also another event occurred, while they were on their way back.

415
00:29:52,623 --> 00:29:56,550
They came on top of this mountain then, there was this valley beneath them.

416
00:29:57,202 --> 00:29:59,604
So, they started making Zikr(زكر) loudly,

417
00:29:59,629 --> 00:30:02,271
Allah O Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah O Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah O Akbar(الله اكبر).

418
00:30:03,284 --> 00:30:04,616
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

419
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:09,423
اِرْبِعُوا عَلَى اَنْفُسِكُمْ يَااَيُّهَاالنَّاسْ اأربعوا على أنفسكم،

420
00:30:10,249 --> 00:30:15,709
فإنكم لا تدعون أصم ولا غائباً، إنما تدعون سميعاً بصيراً

421
00:30:16,004 --> 00:30:22,874
O people restrain yourselves, you're not calling one, who is deaf or one, who is far away,

422
00:30:23,264 --> 00:30:26,965
but you are calling the All Hearing and the All Seeing

423
00:30:28,254 --> 00:30:32,989
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Abu Musa Al-Ashaari(ابوموسى الأشعري) and he was saying,

424
00:30:33,481 --> 00:30:34,975
he was making Zikr(زكر) in his heart,

425
00:30:36,252 --> 00:30:36,780
he was saying;

426
00:30:36,820 --> 00:30:38,768
 لَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّتَ اِلَّا بلله

427
00:30:39,114 --> 00:30:40,710
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

428
00:30:41,253 --> 00:30:48,769
يَا عَبْدَالله بِنْ قَيْسْ قُل لَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّة اِلَّا بِاللهَ،فَاِنَّهَ كَنْزُ مِّنْ كُنُوْز ِالْجَنَّةْ

429
00:30:49,147 --> 00:30:49,647
Say;

430
00:30:49,823 --> 00:30:51,886
لَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّة اِلَّا بِاللهَ

431
00:30:51,926 --> 00:30:54,411
because it's a treasure from Paradise.

432
00:30:55,101 --> 00:30:57,308
So, brothers and sisters we should say;

433
00:30:57,752 --> 00:30:59,822
لَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللهَ

434
00:31:00,107 --> 00:31:03,914
If you want to own a treasure in Jannah(جنة).

435
00:31:04,328 --> 00:31:06,822
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make us the people of Jannah(جنة).

436
00:31:07,175 --> 00:31:10,184
These were the Muslim delegations that Rasool Allah ﷺ received

437
00:31:10,447 --> 00:31:14,507
and then there was one, which was a different case.

438
00:31:14,692 --> 00:31:17,854
And these were from the people of Fazarah(فزارة) from Ghatafaan(غطافان)

439
00:31:18,264 --> 00:31:19,967
these were the allies of the Yahood(أليهود)

440
00:31:20,304 --> 00:31:23,016
and Oyayina Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن), he saw a dream,

441
00:31:23,648 --> 00:31:27,667
he saw that he's taking a mountain called Zur-Ruqaibah(ذوالرقيبة).

442
00:31:28,544 --> 00:31:33,595
He interpreted it, to mean that he would hold on

443
00:31:33,675 --> 00:31:37,316
because, Ar-Raqaibah(الرقيبة) was a small form of Raqabah(رقببة),

444
00:31:37,356 --> 00:31:39,141
Raqabah(رقببة) means neck.

445
00:31:39,408 --> 00:31:46,377
So, he interpreted it, to mean that he would take hold of the neck of Muhammadﷺ and defeat him.

446
00:31:47,287 --> 00:31:52,331
So, he mobilize his people, when he heard that the Muslims have attacked Khaybar(خَيْبَر)

447
00:31:52,688 --> 00:31:56,485
and he came forth to give assistance to his allies Al-Yahood(أليهود).

448
00:31:56,854 --> 00:32:03,750
By the time he reached, Rasool Allah ﷺ has already conquered Khaybar(خَيْبَر) and defeated the Yahood(يهود).

449
00:32:04,029 --> 00:32:07,917
So, this Oyayina Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن) he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him,

450
00:32:08,222 --> 00:32:11,567
hand me over the wealth of my allies

451
00:32:11,607 --> 00:32:14,851
because I took a neutral stand and did not fight you.

452
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:18,742
I mean, look at this liar, he is now saying that I chose not to fight you.

453
00:32:18,862 --> 00:32:21,940
That was not the reason, he came and it was all over.

454
00:32:22,271 --> 00:32:23,637
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

455
00:32:23,677 --> 00:32:28,769
You are a liar you came because of the screaming that you heard in your dreams.

456
00:32:30,143 --> 00:32:32,159
Oyayina Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن) said: Give me something.

457
00:32:32,199 --> 00:32:33,366
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

458
00:32:33,478 --> 00:32:34,871
Go and take the Zur-Ruqaibah(ذوالرقيبة),

459
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:36,223
 he said: What is Zur-Ruqaibah(ذوالرقيبة).?

460
00:32:36,376 --> 00:32:38,229
He said the mountain that you saw in your dream.

461
00:32:38,631 --> 00:32:41,506
I mean this is a barren dry mountain in the middle of nowhere.

462
00:32:41,749 --> 00:32:43,499
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Go and take it.

463
00:32:43,594 --> 00:32:47,247
Oyayina Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن) left angrily, empty handed

464
00:32:47,287 --> 00:32:51,802
and then he met another leader from his people called Al-Haris Bin Auf(ألحارث بن عوف).

465
00:32:52,203 --> 00:32:53,640
Al-Harris(الحارث) told Oyayina(عيينة);

466
00:32:53,906 --> 00:32:57,064
Didn't I tell you, that you wasting your effort for nothing.

467
00:32:57,463 --> 00:33:02,132
Muhammadﷺ will conquer the east and the west.

468
00:33:02,201 --> 00:33:05,147
I was told that by the Rabbi's of the Jews.

469
00:33:05,561 --> 00:33:08,116
They told me that, they see this in their books

470
00:33:08,343 --> 00:33:11,022
that, they would be defeated by Muhammadﷺ.

471
00:33:11,102 --> 00:33:12,284
Didn't I tell you that.

472
00:33:13,399 --> 00:33:17,275
So, Al-Haris Bin Auf(ألحارث بن عوف) had more wisdom than Oyayina Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن)

473
00:33:17,331 --> 00:33:22,297
 and both of them were chiefs of the people of Ghatafaan(غطافان).

474
00:33:22,954 --> 00:33:25,119
We'll talk about Al-Hujjaj Bin Allaat(ألحجاج بن علاط).

475
00:33:25,834 --> 00:33:29,763
Al-Hujjaj Bin Allaat As-Sulami(ألحجاج بن علاط اَلسُّلَمِيْ),

476
00:33:30,459 --> 00:33:33,496
Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج) became Muslim,

477
00:33:34,055 --> 00:33:37,976
and he belongs to the tribe of Bannu Sulaim(بنو سُلَيْم).

478
00:33:38,782 --> 00:33:43,569
And he owned as it says in the books of Seerah(سيرة).

479
00:33:43,593 --> 00:33:48,322
He owned the rights of mining in the land of Sulaim(بنو سُلَيْم).

480
00:33:49,057 --> 00:33:54,371
Now, here mining most likely Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) would refer to the salt mines,

481
00:33:55,164 --> 00:33:58,705
don't think there were any, anything, more developed than that,

482
00:33:58,832 --> 00:34:02,142
it wasn't known in the Arabian Peninsula that, they used to mine for anything else.

483
00:34:03,224 --> 00:34:08,746
So, this is referring to the rights of salt mining in his area.

484
00:34:09,423 --> 00:34:15,601
So, he was a businessman, he was a wealthy man and he had a wife in Makkah.

485
00:34:16,452 --> 00:34:19,851
When he became Muslim, he wanted to collect the money

486
00:34:20,149 --> 00:34:22,108
that was owed to him in Makkah

487
00:34:22,577 --> 00:34:28,321
as a businessman, he would have contracts with a lot of people and they owed him money,

488
00:34:28,361 --> 00:34:33,266
so he wanted to get his money back, before the news spreads that he has become Muslim.

489
00:34:33,306 --> 00:34:36,580
And he was worried that they would confiscate his money.

490
00:34:37,549 --> 00:34:42,225
So, he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said; O Messenger of Allah that people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) owe me money

491
00:34:42,488 --> 00:34:46,673
and I want to go and collect it, would you allow me to speak against you, if I need to.

492
00:34:47,115 --> 00:34:48,138
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

493
00:34:48,288 --> 00:34:49,005
قُلْ مَا بَدَلَكْ

494
00:34:49,045 --> 00:34:50,108
Say whatever you want.

495
00:34:50,893 --> 00:34:53,224
So, Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج) went into Makkah

496
00:34:53,541 --> 00:34:57,128
and this was during the time of Ghazwat-Ul-Khaybar(غزوة الخيبر).

497
00:34:57,497 --> 00:34:59,323
So, he reached to the outskirts of Makkah

498
00:34:59,363 --> 00:35:02,913
and he already found some men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) outside of Makkah(مكه)

499
00:35:03,535 --> 00:35:10,834
waiting for travelers to come in order to ask them about what happened with Rasool Allah ﷺ, in Khaybar(خَيْبَر)?

500
00:35:11,247 --> 00:35:14,951
 They were so eager to know the news of this conflict.

501
00:35:15,427 --> 00:35:17,079
It wasn't like a given for them,

502
00:35:17,755 --> 00:35:23,960
they expected that the Muslims would lose because of the fame of Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

503
00:35:24,597 --> 00:35:28,676
its fortresses, the fighters, the provisions.

504
00:35:29,222 --> 00:35:31,718
Because it was a wealthy area, they had a lot of farms,

505
00:35:32,238 --> 00:35:35,987
they had many fortresses, well built, strong fortresses,

506
00:35:36,201 --> 00:35:40,852
 plus the strongest fighters among Al-Yahood(أليهود), such as Marhab(مرحب) and Yaser(ياسر),

507
00:35:41,294 --> 00:35:44,501
the knights of the Jews were from Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

508
00:35:45,757 --> 00:35:52,155
So, these men would go out during the daytime and wait for the travelers, for the caravans,

509
00:35:52,890 --> 00:35:55,787
in order to ask them, what is happening?

510
00:35:56,483 --> 00:36:05,771
Quite different than how things are today, all news are within reach of the whole globe, within seconds.

511
00:36:06,266 --> 00:36:11,639
With them in the Arabian Peninsula, news would take days to travel.

512
00:36:12,395 --> 00:36:17,623
So, they saw Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج), they knew him because he had a wife from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

513
00:36:18,092 --> 00:36:24,737
So, they said: This is the man we're looking for, he must have information about what has happened.

514
00:36:25,841 --> 00:36:30,663
So, they rushed towards Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج) and they told him tell us about Khaybar(خَيْبَر).

515
00:36:30,967 --> 00:36:31,790
What happened?

516
00:36:32,541 --> 00:36:35,365
He said: I have some very good news for you.

517
00:36:36,002 --> 00:36:39,745
Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج) said: They came to me and they were stuck to my camel.

518
00:36:40,354 --> 00:36:43,948
I mean, you can imagine the scene of him, riding on his camel,

519
00:36:43,988 --> 00:36:49,997
 and these men are so crowded around him, to hear what he has to say that, they were stuck to his camel

520
00:36:50,358 --> 00:36:52,055
and they're all looking up at him.

521
00:36:52,392 --> 00:36:55,944
And then they're going ee, ee, Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج), go ahead Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج), just tell us.

522
00:36:56,694 --> 00:36:59,209
He said Muhammad(محمد) has been defeated

523
00:36:59,921 --> 00:37:02,538
as he has never been defeated before

524
00:37:03,046 --> 00:37:04,878
his companions were killed.

525
00:37:05,192 --> 00:37:07,522
And he was taken as prisoner.

526
00:37:07,847 --> 00:37:09,077
And the Jews said;

527
00:37:09,117 --> 00:37:12,652
We're not going to kill him, but we're going to hand them over to his people in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

528
00:37:12,676 --> 00:37:14,196
so that they kill him inside Makkah.

529
00:37:14,676 --> 00:37:19,743
The enemies of Allah happy, they rushed back to Makkah to carry the news.

530
00:37:20,477 --> 00:37:23,783
And Al-Hajjaj(الحجاج) told them, the only reason, why I came here is

531
00:37:23,823 --> 00:37:26,333
I want to collect my money from you,

532
00:37:26,853 --> 00:37:28,831
so that I can go back to Khaybar(خَيْبَر)

533
00:37:29,180 --> 00:37:33,298
and buy the booty that the Yahood(يهود) won from the Muslims

534
00:37:33,603 --> 00:37:36,968
before all of the other businessmen arrive to Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

535
00:37:37,214 --> 00:37:38,252
and compete with me.

536
00:37:38,596 --> 00:37:42,082
