They were sent in 30 men to Bani Murraa(بني مُرَّة),

721
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:53,922
in an area called Fadak(فدك).

722
00:50:54,407 --> 00:50:58,041
They were surrounded by an overwhelming force

723
00:50:58,446 --> 00:51:00,279
and most of them were killed,

724
00:51:00,644 --> 00:51:10,602
Bashir(بشير) was injured but he was able to retreat and go back to Madina.

725
00:51:11,270 --> 00:51:16,611
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ because of this defeat that Bashir(بشير) and his Sariyyah(سرية) suffered

726
00:51:16,968 --> 00:51:21,281
 he sent out another Sariyyah(سرية) led by Ghalib Bin Abdullah(غالب بن عبدالله),

727
00:51:22,209 --> 00:51:25,916
on the way they met a man called Haris Bin Malik(حارث بن مالك).

728
00:51:26,765 --> 00:51:31,244
Now, this man could be a spy, he could be a traveler, Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم),

729
00:51:31,511 --> 00:51:34,972
so Ghalib(غالب) ordered that he should be arrested.

730
00:51:35,698 --> 00:51:37,612
Haris Bin Malik Al- Laisee(ألحارث بن مالك ألليثي), he said;

731
00:51:38,136 --> 00:51:39,226
اِنَّمَا جِئْتُ مُسْلِمًا

732
00:51:39,551 --> 00:51:41,687
I have come to accept Islam,

733
00:51:42,285 --> 00:51:43,276
Ghalib(غالب) told him;

734
00:51:43,383 --> 00:51:47,071
If you're telling the truth, and you came to really become a Muslim,

735
00:51:47,309 --> 00:51:51,739
then being held a captive for a day and a night wouldn't harm you,

736
00:51:52,126 --> 00:51:55,467
because they only wanted to keep him for a day.

737
00:51:55,843 --> 00:51:58,433
And if you have other motives,

738
00:51:58,997 --> 00:52:01,207
then we are going to take our precautions.

739
00:52:01,578 --> 00:52:03,000
Because if he was a spy,

740
00:52:03,450 --> 00:52:06,003
then he would disclose their location

741
00:52:06,281 --> 00:52:09,315
and their numbers and would give out information to the enemy

742
00:52:09,355 --> 00:52:13,010
and allow them time to mobilize their forces and gather an attack,

743
00:52:13,194 --> 00:52:16,514
see these Sariyyah(سرية), they depended on the element of surprise

744
00:52:16,666 --> 00:52:18,036
because they were very small in number.

745
00:52:18,423 --> 00:52:21,102
And you can see that most of them were ambushes, that were done suddenly,

746
00:52:21,457 --> 00:52:23,312
either at night or early in the morning.

747
00:52:23,543 --> 00:52:25,314
And they take the enemy by surprise.

748
00:52:25,575 --> 00:52:28,623
So, now they were spotted by this man.

749
00:52:28,776 --> 00:52:30,768
So Ghalib(غالب) held him as a captive.

750
00:52:30,815 --> 00:52:34,069
Now, there's a problem here, this man claims that he is a Muslim,

751
00:52:34,310 --> 00:52:38,633
and it's not allowed to take the Muslim for no sin and to arrest him.

752
00:52:39,027 --> 00:52:43,499
But this was the necessary move on part of the leader of the Sariyyah(سرية).

753
00:52:43,823 --> 00:52:46,558
And then he tried to explain it to, this man and told him;

754
00:52:46,769 --> 00:52:51,215
Listen, if you're a Muslim, it won't harm you one time, if you're arrested, if you held captive for one day,

755
00:52:51,930 --> 00:52:54,465
obviously he doesn't want to take this man with them.

756
00:52:54,819 --> 00:52:57,388
He had to leave him in that spot and he left with him.

757
00:52:57,634 --> 00:53:01,100
It says in the narration Rajul Aswad(رجل أسود), a black man,

758
00:53:01,424 --> 00:53:06,856
he gave this man instructions, he told him, if he resists, then cut off his head.

759
00:53:07,774 --> 00:53:13,904
So, they had to hold him where he is, on spot, so that no information is leaked.

760
00:53:14,369 --> 00:53:18,868
It shows you the Hadhar(حذر), the precautions that the Sahabahرضي الله عنهم would take,

761
00:53:18,973 --> 00:53:22,538
they were very intelligent and wise, and they would not be tricked.

762
00:53:23,331 --> 00:53:27,668
They carried on, and Jundub Bin Makeeth(جندب بن مكيث),

763
00:53:28,039 --> 00:53:33,466
he narrates that, he was sent to scout, to spy on the enemy,

764
00:53:33,821 --> 00:53:36,026
because they reached at the time of Asr(عصر).

765
00:53:36,673 --> 00:53:41,449
So, Jundub(جندب), he climbed the hill, or a mountain that overlooks the enemy,

766
00:53:42,057 --> 00:53:46,729
and he took a prone position, laying down stretched off the floor,

767
00:53:46,865 --> 00:53:48,930
 in order that the enemy would not see him.

768
00:53:49,310 --> 00:53:53,652
But one of the men from among the enemy, he spotted Jundub(جندب),

769
00:53:54,196 --> 00:53:57,239
now Jundub(جندب) was laying down in this position without moving.

770
00:53:57,673 --> 00:53:59,607
This man saw him and he told his wife,

771
00:53:59,941 --> 00:54:02,870
I see some dark object on that hill,

772
00:54:03,210 --> 00:54:06,320
go and check if the dogs have taken any of our utensils.

773
00:54:06,360 --> 00:54:09,421
So, she went and checked and didn't see anything missing.

774
00:54:09,461 --> 00:54:11,127
She said, the dogs didn't take anything.

775
00:54:11,159 --> 00:54:14,093
He said: Bring me my bow and my arrows.

776
00:54:14,539 --> 00:54:17,551
So, he took an arrow and he aimed at Jundub(جندب) he shot him

777
00:54:18,141 --> 00:54:20,070
and the arrow hit him.

778
00:54:20,378 --> 00:54:23,393
It says, either in his Jabeen(جبين) or his Janb(جنب).

779
00:54:23,520 --> 00:54:26,060
Jabeen(جبين), means forehead and Janb(جنب) means side,

780
00:54:26,697 --> 00:54:28,163
the narrator wasn't sure.

781
00:54:28,536 --> 00:54:30,126
Anyway, Jundub(جندب) says;

782
00:54:30,412 --> 00:54:36,527
so I pulled out the arrow and put it down slowly, without making any movements.

783
00:54:37,358 --> 00:54:41,179
So, the man then aimed his arrow again and short at Jundub(جندب) another time

784
00:54:41,219 --> 00:54:43,150
 and this time he hit him, in his shoulder.

785
00:54:43,834 --> 00:54:48,384
Jundub(جندب) said: I pulled out the arrow and I placed it, put it down without moving.

786
00:54:48,943 --> 00:54:50,062
So, the man said;

787
00:54:50,328 --> 00:54:52,128
 لَقَدْ خَالَطه سَهْمَائِيْ

788
00:54:52,343 --> 00:54:54,797
My two arrows have definitely struck him.

789
00:54:54,981 --> 00:54:56,681
لَو كَانَ رَبِيْعَتْ لَتَ حَرَّكْ

790
00:54:56,721 --> 00:54:58,793
If, he was a scout he would have moved.

791
00:54:59,068 --> 00:55:01,804
So, you can see the discipline that Jundub(جندب) had,

792
00:55:02,160 --> 00:55:06,892
I mean, being struck twice by these sharp arrows, and is not moving a bit.

793
00:55:07,654 --> 00:55:11,564
He is pulling them slowly, without making any noticeable movement.

794
00:55:12,247 --> 00:55:16,310
So, this man was quite content and comfortable

795
00:55:16,390 --> 00:55:21,619
that this object whatever it is, is not a human being.

796
00:55:22,085 --> 00:55:23,452
And then he told his wife,

797
00:55:23,796 --> 00:55:29,621
tomorrow in the morning, go and collect my two arrows, lest the dogs chew on them.

798
00:55:30,053 --> 00:55:33,591
So, Jundub(جندب) said:, I remained in my position until, it was night time

799
00:55:33,681 --> 00:55:36,922
and their camels and shepherds came back,

800
00:55:37,465 --> 00:55:40,456
and then they had their dinner and they went to sleep,

801
00:55:40,953 --> 00:55:42,797
and that is when we attacked,

802
00:55:43,482 --> 00:55:45,514
so they attacked them, when they were asleep.

803
00:55:45,892 --> 00:55:47,931
He said: We killed some of them.

804
00:55:48,174 --> 00:55:51,780
And then we took all of their camels and whatever,

805
00:55:52,110 --> 00:55:55,566
we took them with us and we made it, away with them.

806
00:55:56,140 --> 00:55:59,778
And then the remaining men who are not killed,

807
00:56:00,462 --> 00:56:03,816
gathered the force and they pursued the Muslims.

808
00:56:04,346 --> 00:56:11,013
Jundub(جندب) says, that the forces that, they gathered were overwhelming huge numbers

809
00:56:11,342 --> 00:56:14,500
and they were pursuing us and they were getting very close to us

810
00:56:14,774 --> 00:56:17,786
and there was no way, we could fight such a number.

811
00:56:18,040 --> 00:56:18,545
He said;

812
00:56:18,627 --> 00:56:20,853
فَجَاؤوْنَا بِمَا لَا قِبَلَ لنَا بِهْ

813
00:56:21,177 --> 00:56:24,428
They brought forces to us that we cannot handle,

814
00:56:24,955 --> 00:56:27,765
he said: While we were running away from them.

815
00:56:28,370 --> 00:56:29,791
We crossed a valley

816
00:56:30,190 --> 00:56:33,738
there was no rain, and there were no conditions for rain.

817
00:56:33,991 --> 00:56:39,568
Nevertheless, Allah brought the flood in this valley that separated us from them

818
00:56:39,924 --> 00:56:46,995
and we would look back and see them all standing on the other side of the valley looking at us, unable to do anything,

819
00:56:47,546 --> 00:56:50,471
and then they made it back safe to Madina.

820
00:56:51,341 --> 00:56:55,793
This story of the Usama(أسامة) is also related within this Sariyyah(سرية)

821
00:56:56,086 --> 00:56:59,015
and it's a famous story, you must have heard of it

822
00:56:59,721 --> 00:57:02,025
and this is the story of a Usama(أسامة) with the man who said;

823
00:57:02,065 --> 00:57:03,179
 لَا اله الَّا الله

824
00:57:03,770 --> 00:57:06,512
There was this man, whenever the enemy would attack,

825
00:57:06,536 --> 00:57:10,272
he would be ahead of them and whenever, they would retreat, he would be the last,

826
00:57:10,772 --> 00:57:14,979
in this Qarr(قر) and Farr(فر) process of fighting of attack and retreat,

827
00:57:15,366 --> 00:57:19,525
this man was ahead in attacking and the last in retreating.

828
00:57:20,005 --> 00:57:22,683
So, he was causing the Muslims some problems,

829
00:57:23,035 --> 00:57:29,106
Usama(أسامة) said: Me and one man from Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), we both made it our objective to, to get him,

830
00:57:29,380 --> 00:57:32,851
so we attacked and when we were within range,

831
00:57:33,457 --> 00:57:33,767
he said;

832
00:57:33,807 --> 00:57:34,838
لَا اله الَّا الله

833
00:57:35,224 --> 00:57:38,585
 So, Usama(أسامة) said: The Ansari(انصاري) stopped

834
00:57:38,910 --> 00:57:42,298
and I carried on and I struck him with my sword and killed him.

835
00:57:42,889 --> 00:57:45,497
The news was carried to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

836
00:57:45,563 --> 00:57:48,582
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was angry and he told Usama(أسامة):

837
00:57:48,795 --> 00:57:51,765
اَقَتَلْتَه’ بَعْدَ اَنْ قَالَ لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

838
00:57:51,918 --> 00:57:53,652
Did you kill him, after he said;

839
00:57:53,732 --> 00:57:55,176
لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

840
00:57:55,517 --> 00:57:59,059
، قَالَ اُسَامَهْ مَا قَالَ هَا اِلَّا مُتَعَوِّذا مِنَّ السَيْفِ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللهَ

841
00:57:59,099 --> 00:58:02,281
He only said it, to seek refuge from the sword.

842
00:58:02,803 --> 00:58:05,816
اَقَتَلْتَه’ بَعْدَ اَنْ قَالَ لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

843
00:58:05,840 --> 00:58:07,155
Did you kill him after he said;

844
00:58:07,179 --> 00:58:08,311
 لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

845
00:58:08,351 --> 00:58:10,821
And he kept on repeating that again and again,

846
00:58:11,021 --> 00:58:14,947
until Usama(أسامة) said: I wished that, I have never became Muslim, except that moment,

847
00:58:16,029 --> 00:58:20,328
and then Usama(أسامة) made a vow that he will never fight anyone in his life.

848
00:58:20,890 --> 00:58:21,324
Who says,

849
00:58:21,364 --> 00:58:22,399
, لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

850
00:58:22,922 --> 00:58:26,216
So, the important lesson here, there are two lessons.

851
00:58:26,838 --> 00:58:30,302
Number one, the sanctity of Muslim blood,

852
00:58:30,998 --> 00:58:36,611
it is the greatest crime after Shirk(شرك) to shed the blood of a Muslim.

853
00:58:37,020 --> 00:58:41,523
And the Ayaat(آيات) of Quran and the Hadith(حديث) show us the danger

854
00:58:42,285 --> 00:58:44,443
and the greatness of this sin,

855
00:58:45,111 --> 00:58:47,787
the one who was murdered would come on the Day of Judgment,

856
00:58:48,047 --> 00:58:50,365
and would hold on to the one who murdered him,

857
00:58:50,706 --> 00:58:54,676
and will say O Allah: Ask this man, why did they spill my blood.

858
00:58:55,459 --> 00:59:02,411
And there is no sin, that our scholars debated whether the Toba(توبة) is accepted or not,

859
00:59:02,451 --> 00:59:04,673
 except with the sin of killing a Muslim.

860
00:59:05,173 --> 00:59:10,974
Now, obviously, the majority view, and the right opinion is that the Toba(توبة) is accepted.

861
00:59:11,184 --> 00:59:12,597
However, it shows you

862
00:59:12,763 --> 00:59:18,184
how dangerous this thing is that it reached to the level that some of them disagreed with this opinion.

863
00:59:18,858 --> 00:59:22,788
So, the blood of one Muslim is sacred.

864
00:59:23,092 --> 00:59:26,433
And the Hadith(حديث) says that it's more sacred than the house of Allah.

865
00:59:27,648 --> 00:59:30,777
The next important lesson, Al-Akhaz Bizzahir(ألأخذ بظاهر)

866
00:59:30,817 --> 00:59:36,622
we take them by what is apparent because in another narration it says,

867
00:59:36,778 --> 00:59:38,273
هَلَّا شَقَقْتَ عن قَلْبِه

868
00:59:38,358 --> 00:59:43,193
Why didn't you split his heart open to see what is in it?

869
00:59:43,857 --> 00:59:45,565
Have you opened up his heart

870
00:59:46,146 --> 00:59:48,129
to know whether he was a Muslim or not?

871
00:59:48,168 --> 00:59:49,438
Whether he was honestly saying

872
00:59:49,478 --> 00:59:50,256
لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

873
00:59:50,296 --> 00:59:52,702
or he was saying it just to seek refuge from the sword?

874
00:59:52,750 --> 00:59:53,536
How do you know?

875
00:59:53,758 --> 00:59:56,837
So we go by Az'zahir(ألظاهر), we go by what we see.

876
00:59:57,349 --> 01:00:01,423
If a person claims to be a Muslim, then we take him for his word,

877
01:00:01,463 --> 01:00:06,004
and we leave As-Saraaer(أَلسَّرَائِرْ), we leave what is in the hearts to Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the Day of Judgment.

878
01:00:06,234 --> 01:00:08,293
Now, this applies both ways,

879
01:00:09,085 --> 01:00:11,071
this applies to go Kuffr(كفر) and applies to Eeman(اِيْمان),

880
01:00:11,630 --> 01:00:16,455
if what we see from a person is Kuffr(كفر), then we judge them as being disbelievers.

881
01:00:16,495 --> 01:00:21,483
If what we see from a person apparently is Eeman(اِيْمان) and Islam, then we judge them to be Muslim.

882
01:00:22,588 --> 01:00:26,336
We did not dig into their hearts and try to find out what's in them.

883
01:00:27,348 --> 01:00:30,581
Same thing here, we could also look at the lesson of Jundub(جندب),

884
01:00:31,259 --> 01:00:33,552
when he took this man as a prisoner, he said,

885
01:00:34,173 --> 01:00:36,107
when that man said that I'm a Muslim.

886
01:00:36,265 --> 01:00:40,475
Jundub(جندب) did not try to argue with that and say you're lying, you're a spy,

887
01:00:40,816 --> 01:00:45,217
No, He told him, if you're a Muslim then have Sabr(صبر) and patience for one day,

888
01:00:45,664 --> 01:00:47,233
if you're not than Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم).

889
01:00:47,749 --> 01:00:50,986
Next Sariyyah(سرية), Sariyyah Abi Hadrad(سرية أبي حدرد).

890
01:00:51,529 --> 01:00:54,698
Abi Hazrad(أبي حدرد) got married to a woman from his people

891
01:00:55,272 --> 01:01:00,787
and he promise pay a dowry of 200 Dirham(درهم).

892
01:01:01,253 --> 01:01:04,119
So, he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him, O Rasool Ullah, help me,

893
01:01:04,178 --> 01:01:07,085
I mean he offered to pay this Mahar(مهر) but didn't have the money,

894
01:01:07,754 --> 01:01:09,246
so he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

895
01:01:09,286 --> 01:01:15,594
O Messenger of Allah, I got married and I promise to pay 200 Dirham(درهم) as Mahar(مهر).

896
01:01:15,747 --> 01:01:16,806
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

897
01:01:16,905 --> 01:01:22,788
 سبحان الله وَلله لَوْ كُنْتُمْ تَاخُذُوْنَهَا مِنْ وَّادٍّ مَّا زَادْ، وللهِ مَا عِنْدِيْ مَااُعِيْنُكَ بِهْ

898
01:01:23,337 --> 01:01:24,353
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

899
01:01:24,440 --> 01:01:30,932
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), if you were picking up money from a stream, you wouldn't have paid more,

900
01:01:31,585 --> 01:01:33,887
in the name of Allah, I have nothing to help you with.

901
01:01:34,077 --> 01:01:37,658
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw this as a lot of money to pay as Mahar(مهر),

902
01:01:38,216 --> 01:01:41,166
and he said, if money was flowing in a stream

903
01:01:41,764 --> 01:01:44,879
you wouldn't have offered to pay more than what you have paid.

904
01:01:45,532 --> 01:01:50,212
Anyway later on Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Hazrad(ابوحدرد) along with two men

905
01:01:50,755 --> 01:01:59,917
to go and check out what's going on with a particular man, who was gathering a force to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ.

906
01:01:59,957 --> 01:02:00,779
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told them:

907
01:02:00,901 --> 01:02:05,018
اُخُرجُوْ اِلَى هَذَا الرَّجُلْ حَتَّى تَأتُوهُمْ مِنْه’بِخَبَرِ وَّ عِلْمْ

908
01:02:05,763 --> 01:02:10,616
This man is Qais(قيس), he was gathering force to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ

909
01:02:11,379 --> 01:02:14,949
and he sent Abu Hazrad(ابوحدرد) along with two men, to find out what's happening.

910
01:02:15,597 --> 01:02:17,572
وَقَدَّمَ لَنَا شَارِفًا اَجْفَا

911
01:02:18,131 --> 01:02:21,996
He gave us a weak old camel, and told them.

912
01:02:22,036 --> 01:02:23,125
تَبَلَّغُ عَلَى هَذِه

913
01:02:23,173 --> 01:02:24,148
Make do with her.

914
01:02:24,383 --> 01:02:28,959
Now the situation of this camel was pretty bad, and she wasn't even working

915
01:02:29,502 --> 01:02:32,959
When one of them was riding on the camel, she couldn't even stand up.

916
01:02:33,298 --> 01:02:36,842
Abu Hazrad(ابوحدرد) said, that we had to push it, from behind to have her stand up.

917
01:02:37,511 --> 01:02:39,678
So, this camel was a very bad situation.

918
01:02:40,268 --> 01:02:46,497
That's all what Rasool Allah ﷺ was able to offer them, this weak old camel.

919
01:02:47,462 --> 01:02:53,375
So, they traveled three of them, with this weak camel, they arrived at night

920
01:02:53,823 --> 01:02:56,423
and Abu Hazrad(ابوحدرد) said: I took my position.

921
01:02:56,946 --> 01:03:00,467
And I ordered my two companions to hide in another spot

922
01:03:01,211 --> 01:03:05,620
and then he gave them orders, when you hear my Takbeer(تكبير), make your move.

923
01:03:06,304 --> 01:03:09,411
So, he said I was waiting for an opportunity, Gharrah(غرَّه).

924
01:03:09,970 --> 01:03:12,919
And no opportunity came yet.

925
01:03:13,441 --> 01:03:18,301
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ, His Qadar(قدر), their Shepherd was late,

926
01:03:18,726 --> 01:03:21,076
 shepherd of these Kuffar(كفار), he was late.

927
01:03:21,392 --> 01:03:25,140
So Qais(قيس) said: I'm going to go and try to find him.

928
01:03:25,793 --> 01:03:27,278
His people said, Let us go.

929
01:03:27,820 --> 01:03:30,363
He said: No, in the name of Allah, No one will go with me.

930
01:03:30,417 --> 01:03:32,295
They said: Then let us come with you.

931
01:03:32,395 --> 01:03:34,069
He said: No, I'm going to go alone.

932
01:03:34,655 --> 01:03:40,072
Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah, He walked alone looking for his shepherd

933
01:03:40,740 --> 01:03:44,201
and he comes right in front of Abu Hazrad(ابوحدرد).

934
01:03:44,978 --> 01:03:48,338
Abu Hazrad(ابوحدرد) said: When he was within range,

935
01:03:48,571 --> 01:03:52,965
I shot an arrow at him piercing him in the heart.

936
01:03:53,690 --> 01:03:59,758
He said: I swear, he did not utter a sound he drop down dead without making a sound.

937
01:04:00,254 --> 01:04:02,350
I jumped at him, and cut off his head.

938
01:04:02,580 --> 01:04:07,432
And then I made my takbeer(تكبير) and my two companions made their takbeer(تكبير) and we attacked

939
01:04:07,881 --> 01:04:11,753
and the kuffar(كفار) were in a disarray, they were running in every direction.

940
01:04:12,063 --> 01:04:15,922
We took all of their camels and we made it, we went back to Madina.

941
01:04:16,049 --> 01:04:18,568
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave me 13 camels.

942
01:04:18,752 --> 01:04:20,487
So, I concluded my marriage.

943
01:04:20,952 --> 01:04:26,340
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

